    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nmy Problem is this\n\nI'm using Neovim's built-in `vim.pack` to install approximately 27 plugins from GitHub.\n\nDuring the initial installation, several Git clone operations remain stalled for an extended period. Neovim eventually reports a timeout and aborts configuration loading.\n\nThe error includes:\nE5108: Lua: /usr/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/_async.lua:53: timeout\nstack traceback:\n    [C]: in function 'assert'\n    /usr/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/_async.lua:53: in function 'wait'\n    /usr/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/pack.lua:520: in function 'async_join_run_wait'\n    /usr/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/pack.lua:557: in function 'run_list'\n    /usr/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/pack.lua:1313: in function 'update'\n\nI also encountered a similar timeout during `vim.pack.add()`.\n\nObserved behavior\n\nGit processes for plugins including `lualine.nvim`, `nvim-web-devicons`, and `snacks.nvim` remained running with negligible CPU usage for nearly two minutes.\n\nNeovim subsequently timed out, preventing normal configuration loading. A subsequent startup also reported that `mason-lspconfig` could not be found.\n\n\nRelated issue\n\nThis appears related to [[#36199](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/36199)](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/36199), addressed by [[PR #36992](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/36992)](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/36992), which increased the default timeout to two minutes.\n\nEnvironment\n\n- Operating system: Arch Linux\n- Neovim version: \nNVIM v0.12.6\nBuild type: RelWithDebInfo\nLuaJIT 2.1.1792588164\n- Git version: git version 2.56.0\n- Installation method: sudo pacman -S neovim\n- Internet connection: my internet is 15MB/s\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Configure `vim.pack.add()` with approximately 27 GitHub plugin repositories.\n2. Start Neovim with plugins not yet installed.\n3. Allow the initial installation to run .\n4. Observe the timeout and incomplete plugin installation.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n\nPlugin installation should handle slow or stalled downloads gracefully, report which repositories failed, and allow failed downloads to be retried without requiring a complete installation to restart.\n\nIt would also be useful to allow the installation timeout to be configured, or to handle timeouts and retries per plugin rather than aborting the entire operation.\n\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\n0.12.6\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno, 9.2.1178\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nArchlinux latest\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nKitty latest\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-256color\n\n### Installation\n\nsystem package manager",
